@oxynote/lezer-logsql
Copyright 2026 Oxynote

This package is a Lezer grammar for LogsQL, the query language of
VictoriaLogs. The grammar, its tokenizer and the tooling around them are
Oxynote's own work, distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The grammar follows the parser of VictoriaLogs:

  https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaLogs/blob/master/lib/logstorage/parser.go

VictoriaLogs is Copyright 2019-2026 VictoriaMetrics, Inc. and is
distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaLogs/blob/master/LICENSE

The parts below come from VictoriaLogs.

In the published package:

  - src/keywords.ts (dist/keywords.js): the names of the pipes and
    functions, read from the parser's source in
    https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaLogs/tree/master/lib/logstorage

In the repository only:

  - upstream/keywords.json: the same names, and every keyword the parser
    checks.
  - upstream/queries.json: queries from the tests in
    https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaLogs/tree/master/lib/logstorage
    (the *_test.go files) and from the examples in
    https://github.com/VictoriaMetrics/VictoriaLogs/blob/master/docs/victorialogs/logsql.md
    Each query is stored with the verdict of a VictoriaLogs server, and an
    invalid one with the server's error message.
  - test/victorialogs-answers.json: the verdicts and error messages a
    VictoriaLogs server gave on this repository's own test queries. The
    queries are Oxynote's own.
  - test/accepted-invalid.txt: queries from the two files above, with the
    same error messages.

scripts/sync-upstream.ts rewrites the files under upstream/ from a
VictoriaLogs release.
